        <obo:IAO_0000115>A penicillanic acid compound having a (6R)-amino substituent. The active nucleus common to all penicillins, it may be substituted at the 6-amino position to form the semisynthetic penicillins, resulting in a variety of antibacterial and pharmacologic characteristics.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>KEGG:C02954</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PDBeChem:X1E</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
