            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A glycosylglucose disaccharide, found most notably in milk, that consists of D-galactose and D-glucose fragments bonded through a beta-1-&gt;4 glycosidic linkage. The glucose fragment can be in either the alpha- or beta-pyranose form, whereas the galactose fragment can only have the beta-pyranose form.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GlyGen:G74621DY</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GlyTouCan:G74621DY</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
