        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33916"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any aldopentose where the open-chain form has all the hydroxy groups on the same side in the Fischer projection. Occurrs in two enantiomeric forms, D- and L-ribose, of which only the former is found in nature.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ribo-pentose</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
