        <obo:IAO_0000115>An interneuron that has its cell body in a central nervous system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Interneurons are commonly described as being only found in the central nervous system. However, in CL we define &apos;interneuron&apos; more broadly as any neuron that is neither a motor neuron nor a sensory neuron, regardless of its location, so we need this term to refer strictly to interneurons of the central nervous system.</rdfs:comment>
