            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An immature B cell of an intermediate stage between the pre-B cell stage and the mature naive stage with the phenotype surface IgM-positive and CD19-positive, and are subject to the process of B cell selection. A transitional B cell migrates from the bone marrow into the peripheral circulation, and then to the spleen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transitional B cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transitional stage B lymphocyte</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transitional stage B-cell</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>transitional stage B-lymphocyte</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>T1 B cell</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>T2 B cell</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>T3 B cell</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for &apos;transitional B cell&apos;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>transitional stage B cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
