        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0042110"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which a precursor cell type acquires characteristics of a more mature T-cell. A T cell is a type of lymphocyte whose definin characteristic is the expression of a T cell receptor complex.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>T lymphocyte differentiation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>T-cell differentiation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>T-lymphocyte differentiation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>T cell development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that the term &apos;thymocyte differentiation&apos; was merged into this term because thymocytes are T cells, and thus the term was essentially redundant. Note that immunologists typically use the word &apos;development&apos; to refer to cells of B or T cell lineages undergoing the process that GO describes as &apos;cell differentiation&apos;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>T cell differentiation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0030217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The process in which a precursor cell type acquires characteristics of a more mature T-cell. A T cell is a type of lymphocyte whose definin characteristic is the expression of a T cell receptor complex.</owl:annotatedTarget>
