            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Progression through the phases of the meiotic cell cycle, in which canonically a cell replicates to produce four offspring with half the chromosomal content of the progenitor cell via two nuclear divisions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Meiosis</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>meiosis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that this term should not be confused with &apos;GO:0140013 ; meiotic nuclear division&apos;. &apos;GO:0051321 ; meiotic cell cycle represents the entire mitotic cell cycle, while &apos;GO:0140013 meiotic nuclear division&apos; specifically represents the actual nuclear division step of the mitotic cell cycle.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>meiotic cell cycle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
