        <obo:IAO_0000115>An embolus (that is, an abnormal particle circulating in the blood) located in the pulmonary artery and thereby blocking blood circulation to the lung. Usually the embolus is a blood clot that has developed in an extremity (for instance, a deep venous thrombosis), detached, and traveled through the circulation before becoming trapped in the pulmonary artery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SNOMEDCT_US:59282003</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0034065</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
