        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Oncological abnormality</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Tumor</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Tumour</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Oncology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>The World Health Organization (WHO) classifies neoplasms into four main groups: (i) benign neoplasm, (ii) in situ neoplasm, (iii) malignant neoplasm, and (iv) neoplasm of uncertain or unknown behavior. A malignant neoplasm is also known as cancer.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Neoplasm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
