        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>treatment with retinoid therapy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>A retinoic acid agent binds to and/or activates specific nuclear retinoic acid receptors (RARs) and retinoid X receptors (RXRs), thereby modulating transcription of genes responsible for cell differentiation and proliferation. A retinoic acid agent may exhibit immunomodulatory and anti-inflammatory properties and may inhibit ornithine decarboxylase, resulting in a decrease in polyamine synthesis and keratinization.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">retinoid agent therapy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


