        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>WXS</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>exome sequencing</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>whole exome sequencing</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Clinical Exome Sequencing is a test for identifying disease-causing DNA variants within the 1% of the genome which codes for proteins (exons) or flanks the regions which code for proteins (splice junctions).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Sequence analysis of the exons of protein-coding genes in the genome typically performed by target enrichment or capture of exons followed by next-generation sequencing.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">clinical whole-exome sequencing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0009004"/>
