            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>One of the three blood vessels, usually one large umbilical vein and two small umbilical arteries, buried within Wharton&apos;s jelly, that transport blood to and from the placenta, where exchange between the mother and fetus takes place; the umbilical vein carries oxygenated, nutrient-rich blood from the placenta to the fetus, and the umbilical arteries carry deoxygenated, nutrient-depleted blood from the fetus to the placenta.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:36493</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:408728001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>allantoic vessel</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>umbilical cord blood vessel</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>umbilical vessel</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>umbilical cord blood vessels</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>umbilical vasculature</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>umbilical blood vessel</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
